Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:30:07 +0800
Subject: session-ui/message: turn stats in the reply's meta line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a turn finishes, the line under the reply reads e.g.
"1m 14s · ttft 480ms · 42 t/s · 95% cache · $0.23":
- the duration, as before;
- time to first token and tokens per second of the last model call that produced
  output (from time.output, patch core/first-output-time). t/s is left out when
  the output took under a second: providers sometimes deliver a short reply in one
  burst, which would read as thousands of tokens per second;
- the share of prompt tokens read from the cache and the cost, summed over every
  step of the turn. Cost is left out when the model has no prices.
Short labels so it fits one line on a phone.

Ocelot-Patch: web/turn-stats

